# The course's values. Copy to course.env, fill in, upload with the hooks.
#
# voclib.sh sources this out of /voc/scripts before any hook runs and exports
# everything in it, so voclab.py reads these as its own environment. Every key
# here is optional: a course that sets none of them gets a working single-node
# cluster with no libraries, no catalog, no notebooks and no warehouse. A key
# left blank counts as unset, so an unfilled line is the same as a missing one.
#
# This file is sourced by bash, so a value carrying spaces needs quoting and
# nothing here may be a command. Names are VOC_COURSE_*, which is the prefix
# voc_report_env excludes: these are the course's values, not Vocareum's, and
# mixing them into that measurement would make it useless.
#
# Nothing secret belongs here. It is uploaded to /voc/scripts on a host students
# share, and voc_report_env prints VOC_ variables to the console log. A
# credential for an external service goes in a Databricks secret scope created by
# workspace_init.sh, and the hook reads it from there.

# --- The student's cluster -------------------------------------------------

# Databricks runtime. Default is 17.3.x-scala2.13, which is not an ML runtime:
# an ML build is several minutes slower to boot, so a course that needs one says
# so here rather than paying for it without knowing.
#VOC_COURSE_SPARK_VERSION=17.3.x-cpu-ml-scala2.13

# Node shape for the single node. Default is i3.xlarge, 4 cores and 30.5 GB,
# which is what the built-in Personal Compute policy would give a student who
# made their own cluster.
#VOC_COURSE_NODE_TYPE=i3.xlarge

# The catalog the cluster opens in. No default, because a catalog name nobody
# asked for is a catalog that does not exist and a cluster whose initial catalog
# is missing fails at the first cell rather than at create.
#VOC_COURSE_CATALOG=workshop

# Idle minutes before the cluster stops. Default is 90, sized to clear a
# scheduled break: a student who comes back to a terminated cluster waits the
# full 16 minutes for it again, which costs more than the idle time does.
#VOC_COURSE_AUTOTERMINATION_MINUTES=90

# What to install on the cluster. One kind:value per line or per comma, kind one
# of pypi, maven, cran, jar, whl. The kind is split off at the first colon only,
# which is what lets a Maven coordinate keep its own two.
#
# Every library here is time a student waits: measured, a cluster reaches RUNNING
# in about 10 minutes and eleven libraries take another 6 to reach INSTALLED.
#VOC_COURSE_LIBRARIES="pypi:neo4j==6.2.0, maven:org.neo4j:neo4j-connector-apache-spark_2.13:5.4.3_for_spark_3"

# --- What the student is handed -------------------------------------------

# The notebooks imported into the student's workspace folder, comma or
# whitespace separated. Names of files or of directories, uploaded to
# /voc/scripts beside the hooks; a directory contributes every .ipynb, .py,
# .sql, .scala and .r under it at any depth, keeping the relative path.
#
# The first file of the first name is where the student lands, so the order here
# chooses the landing page. Naming nothing imports nothing, which is a real
# course and not an error.
#VOC_COURSE_NOTEBOOKS=notebooks

# --- The SQL warehouse ----------------------------------------------------

# Created by workspace_init.sh, once per workspace, only when this name is set.
# It exists because the Statement Execution API takes a warehouse_id and there
# is no other way to run SQL from a hook. A course that runs no SQL leaves this
# unset and no warehouse is created.
#
# Nothing here ever deletes it. Like the instance pool it is instructor-owned,
# and docs/pre-warm.md is where a class is told to go looking for one left
# running after the room has emptied.
#VOC_COURSE_WAREHOUSE_NAME=workshop-warehouse

# Size and idle timeout. Defaults are 2X-Small and 10 minutes. The warehouse is
# serverless, so the first statement after an auto-stop waits seconds rather
# than the several minutes a classic warehouse takes to come back, which is what
# makes a short timeout affordable in a workshop that alternates between talking
# and running.
#VOC_COURSE_WAREHOUSE_SIZE=2X-Small
#VOC_COURSE_WAREHOUSE_AUTO_STOP_MINUTES=10
